\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Overall architecture of the Cryptographic Coprocessor. Ordinary transactions remain on the EVM execution path. Calls recognized by the Identity Hooks enter the coprocessor boundary, where the dispatcher selects a prepared WASM module through version metadata. Upgrade proposals are published on chain, while the Upgrade Handler verifies, compiles, and instantiates WASM modules before the Activation Block makes a prepared version active.}}{6}{figure.3.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:overview}{{1}{6}{Overall architecture of the Cryptographic Coprocessor. Ordinary transactions remain on the EVM execution path. Calls recognized by the Identity Hooks enter the coprocessor boundary, where the dispatcher selects a prepared WASM module through version metadata. Upgrade proposals are published on chain, while the Upgrade Handler verifies, compiles, and instantiates WASM modules before the Activation Block makes a prepared version active}{figure.3.1}{}}
